std::function&lt;std::shared_ptr&lt;storage::ITensorStorageBackend&gt;()&gt;</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>BackendFactory</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::tensor::TensorCoreStorageBridge::BackendFactory</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Injectable factory for the default storage backend (STUB #269). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Signature: <computeroutput>std::shared_ptr&lt;ITensorStorageBackend&gt; factory()</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>When set, the factory is called during <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_core_storage_bridge" kindref="compound">TensorCoreStorageBridge</ref></computeroutput> construction whenever no explicit backend is provided. This allows the production bootstrap to inject a <computeroutput>RocksDBTensorBackend</computeroutput> without every call site needing to know the concrete type.</para>
<para>Typical production bootstrap (main_server.cpp): <programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_core_storage_bridge_1a99f8409f2d33fabb7a2a616cb5253af7" kindref="member">TensorCoreStorageBridge::setDefaultBackendFactory</ref>([&amp;]<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>std::make_shared&lt;RocksDBTensorBackend&gt;(db_handle);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Tests that need an in-memory backend simply omit this call (factory is null → constructor falls back to <computeroutput>InMemoryTensorBackend</computeroutput>). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
